| `agents.editable_names.<name>` | string | `README.md`, with its reason | a bare file name or an `fnmatch` glob over one (no `/`, not `.` or `..`) mapped to a non-blank reason; empty for no carve-out | `scripts/apply_refactor.py` (`load_policy`, `protected_by`) | Carves the name back out of a protected directory, so an agent may edit, for example, `scripts/README.md`; the file's realpath is judged too, so a link named `README.md` to a protected file is still refused. | protecting a file: `agents.protected_names` | always |
